 "objective": "Kernel-grade audit of the self-implication / conclusion-as-hypothesis pattern found textually by the fourth-invocation independent semantic review (V4): for every theorem declared in the two import-disjoint audit partitions, decide with the kernel (isDefEq on the elaborated type, not pretty-printed text) whether the theorem's type is a self-implication P -> P (or P <-> P), whether the conclusion occurs among the hypotheses, or whether the type is otherwise vacuous given its own hypotheses. Classify each hit: tautology (proves nothing, no axiom), genuine implication used downstream, or statement defect; record the axiom cone, module, source line and proof-level downstream consumers. Produce the exact remediation list with an owning task per hit. Do not edit release/ sources; audit is read-only and emits a machine-readable report plus a short card.",
 "deps": [
  "baseline/v4-independent/review.json (V4 full-population textual screen: 1 hit) and baseline/v4-independent/fake_screen2.py",
  "baseline/c1/logs/frozen-type-audit-G{1,2}.log (12,543 declaration rows with pretty-printed types)",
  "baseline/audit/AxiomAudit_G{1,2}.lean (frozen partition definition; reuse the import-disjoint partition)",
  "release/Poincare/D7/SurgeryFlow/Basic.lean:277-279 (the one textual hit: realLineProcedureChain_simplyConnected : P -> P)"
 ],
 "lane": "verifier",
 "acceptance": "Constructed input: a Lean driver that imports each partition and, for every theorem in it, elaborates the type and runs isDefEq between each hypothesis and the conclusion (and syntactically detects P -> P); its output is a per-declaration verdict table over all 12,543 rows / 7,655 theorems, not a sample. Downstream consumer: the audit report is consumed by the D9-disclosure line and by the owner of any repaired declaration; the one known hit must be reproduced or explicitly refuted with the kernel. Independent rebuild: a second, independent tool path (e.g. Lean.Meta.isDefEq via a different traversal or `#check`-based type parsing plus a def-eq probe) reproduces the hit set, and the sampled V4 screen is reconciled against the full screen. Semantic review: each hit is classified tautology / genuine / defect with its cone and downstream consumers, explicitly separated from soundness (a tautology with a clean cone is a disclosure item, not an inconsistency), and the card ends TASK_DONE/TASK_BLOCKED. Scope note: this is a finite-model Lean package; no Poincare/Perelman claim.",
 "host_pool": [
  "ophis-gpu"
 ],
 "requires_lean": true,
 "max_hours": 6,
 "expected_evidence": "kernel def-eq screen driver + exit code, full verdict table over all 7,655 theorems, hit list with cones/consumers/source lines, independent-tool-path replay, result card under longrun/results/",
 "created_by": "L1-lean-baseline",
 "created_at": "2026-09-11T17:30:00Z",
 "notes": "New scope created by the fourth invocation's independent V4 review (finding F10). Not a duplicate: L5-C1-a3-d2-counterexample audits CurvatureODE headline theorems by counterexample in a fresh namespace; D9-adversarial-audit-release screened 596 D2/D3 declarations; V4's full-population textual screen covered all 7,655 theorem types but could not decide definitional equality, and found exactly one textual hit in D7, outside D13 StatementAudit's D11/D12/VKPort-only scope (3,196 theorems). The task's forbidden list includes fake/weakened theorems, so this pattern must be enumerated exhaustively rather than sampled."
